        why: "Each declared view slot keeps a bounded set of possible receiver, parameter, or static sources through every return path, call, generic instantiation, aggregate projection, function value, lambda, and trait implementation. Every possible owner must stay live; a consumed (`&&`) parameter or receiver is freed when the function returns, so it never owns a returned view.",
